      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1900, the Missouri Fish Commissioner stocked the spring-fed stream with 40,000 mountain trout, turning it into a fishing hotspot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://mostateparks.com/page/bennett-spring-state-park/park-history-bennett-spring",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the 1930s, the Civilian Conservation Corps built cabins, a shelter house, roads, trails, an arched bridge, and a rustic dining lodge that still define the park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
